<p>Myanmar&#x27;s military-backed authorities said detained former leader Aung San Suu Kyi has been moved from prison to house arrest at a designated residence, more than five years after the army seized power from her elected government on Feb. 1, 2021. State media said President Min Aung Hlaing commuted the remaining portion of the 80-year-old Nobel laureate&#x27;s sentence to house arrest. The move followed a prisoner amnesty marking the Full Moon Day of Kason, a Buddhist holiday honoring Buddha&#x27;s birthday; the amnesty covered 1,519 prisoners, including 11 foreigners, and cut remaining prison terms by one sixth. Suu Kyi was originally sentenced to 33 years in prison in late 2022 on offenses that her supporters and rights groups described as politically motivated, and the latest reductions would leave her sentence at about 18 years with more than 13 years left to serve, according to calculations in AP-based accounts. Her exact location remained undisclosed after the announcement, and there was no independent confirmation of her condition.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/74NEO778UfhKY2jiHxVBHOI8f8hbqsYaRk0JSHgxSwXsI8pf4vpZyY6Sfd3KbXf-GepusJ-b6rEsE_1tvG0pYI7sJKBnVfLwq2cIrzkcG6DlxGPZeVORhy4axEM5uvO8DPEFayENp6qH5r_iIfPszzP3yGXMQ8xoYv8sdAVYTh4bRGTsA3qEFgUXQlpyonGDOT2qHV3sJHi1Pv2_Hj4Ib980LH1ulrP7aFaMoGVw8Xl3_GHIojTFMeMzJGNTdwcBhGypq8Wt8Ta7lMghUN_X7tnpfeY3' alt='Aung San Suu Kyi has been moved from prison to house arrest.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Public image: State media&#x27;s photograph was described as the first official public image of Suu Kyi in years.</li><li>Possible whereabouts: Kleine Zeitung described her current holding place as secret and probably in the capital, Naypyidaw.</li><li>Legal access: Malaysia&#x27;s Berita Harian said Suu Kyi&#x27;s legal team planned to seek a meeting with her during the weekend after the transfer.</li><li>Detention record: Before the 2021 coup, Suu Kyi had spent a total of 15 years under house arrest during earlier periods of military rule.</li></ul><blockquote>I still do not know where my mother is. I do not know how she is. I remain deeply concerned about whether she is still alive - Kim Aris</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Myanmar military-backed authorities: The official announcement described the move as clemency for Buddha Day, saying it showed humanitarian concern and the “kindness of the state.” (<a href='https://www.gnlm.com.mm/daw-aung-san-suu-kyi-moved-to-designated-residence-to-serve-remaining-sentence/'>Global New Light of Myanmar</a>)</li><li>Kim Aris: Suu Kyi&#x27;s son questioned whether the state-media image proved anything current, saying the photo appeared to date from 2022. (<a href='https://www.nrk.no/nyheter/fredsprisvinner-aung-san-suu-kyi-overfort-til-husarrest-1.17868052'>NRK</a>)</li><li>United Nations: U.N. spokesperson Stephane Dujarric said the commutation was a meaningful step toward conditions for a credible political process, and said a viable political solution required an immediate cessation of violence and inclusive dialogue. (<a href='https://tribune.com.pk/story/2605807/suu-kyi-to-be-moved-to-house-arrest'>The Express Tribune</a>)</li><li>Democracy monitors: Monitors described the sentence reductions as a rebranding of military rule intended to improve the government&#x27;s image. (<a href='https://www.ucanews.com/news/myanmar-junta-reduces-prison-sentences-shortens-suu-kyis-detention/113077'>UCA News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/aung-san-suu-kyi-moved-from-prison-to-house-arrest-in-myanmar-11434040#publisher=newsstand'>Aung San Suu Kyi Moved From Prison To House Arrest In Myanmar</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/30/g-s1-119543/myanmar-junta-says-suu-kyi-moved-to-house-arrest-doubts-linger'>Myanmar junta says Suu Kyi moved to house arrest, doubts linger</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/aung-san-suu-ky